{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793377552,"nonce":"FE7WfO8VtQYqGkhPmtfcqZbh1oU=","message":"Revision: use Haxe's existing display-mode convention instead of a new `@:ide.completion` metadata channel.\n\nIn Haxe, a macro learns where the editor cursor is through `Compiler.getDisplayPos()`, `Context.containsDisplayPosition(pos)` and `Context.getDisplayMode()`. It then returns an expression positioned at the cursor, either a parsed slice or `EDisplay(e, DKDot | DKStructure | DKMarked | DKCall)`, and the compiler's ordinary completion answers. Ashui's `Markup.displayed` already does this for `{expr}`; tink_hxx/coconut map attributes to a structure literal typed against the props type, so prop completion comes from the typer with generics substituted.\n\nRayzor gaps:\n- `containsDisplayPosition` is hardcoded false (context_api.rs);\n- `getDisplayPos` / `getDisplayMode` are not implemented;\n- `EDisplay` is unwrapped and discarded (expr_adt.rs);\n- the LSP never runs macros in display mode with the cursor position, so nothing reaches completion.\n\nPlan:\n1. The LSP runs macro expansion for the edited file in display mode: it sets the display position and mode, implements the three Context/Compiler calls, and keeps `EDisplay` through typing, answering completion at its position by kind.\n2. Ashui extends `displayed` for tags and attributes:\n   - attributes become an `EDisplay(DKStructure)` structure literal typed against the component's props (built-ins against a typedef built from Prop/HANDLERS);\n   - tags become `EDisplay(DKDot)` on a type listing the tags.\n3. Kebab-case names (`card-header`, Tw classes) are not Haxe identifiers. They need quoted structure fields or an enum abstract whose string values Rayzor offers as `textEdit`s with a dash-aware replace range. Tw class strings have no Haxe convention; the descriptor provider stays only for them.\n\nRayzor work order is unchanged: a tolerant markup scanner and display-mode macros first.","files":null}]}